letely surrounded by South Africa from 1910. Though the Basotho (then known as Basuto) and their territory had been under British control starting in 1868 (and ruled by Cape Colony from 1871), the rule by Cape Colony was unpopular and unable to control the territory. As a result, Basutoland was brought under direct authority of Queen Victoria, via the High Commissioner, and run by an Executive Council presided over by a series of British Resident Commissioners.\nIt was divided into seven administrative districts: Berea, Leribe, Maseru, Mohale's Hoek, Mafeteng, Qacha's Nek and Quthing."}],"facts":[{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"capital","value_qid":"Q3909","value_label":"Maseru","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P36","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Maseru"},{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"official_language","value_qid":"Q1860","value_label":"English","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P37","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"English"},{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"religion","value_qid":"Q5043","value_label":"Christianity","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P140","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"Christianity"},{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"government","value_qid":"Q1351282","value_label":"crown colony","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P122","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":"crown colony"},{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"flag","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Unofficial flag of Basutoland.svg","from_t":1951,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P41","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null},{"qid":"Q2340665","kind":"coat","value_qid":null,"value_label":"Coat of arms of Basutoland (1951–1966).svg","from_t":null,"to_t":null,"title":null,"property":"P94","retrieved":"2026-10-30","vl":null}],"people":{},"media":{"Unofficial flag of Basutoland.svg":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Unofficial_flag_of_Basutoland.svg/330px-Unofficial_flag_of_Basutoland.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_con